      "math_academy_id": "e-432",
      "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^5 f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\\,?$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284587/assets/94a33020cd8dd259778c31de4ff49dfe3e210b248260f30d55c6f117defea0de.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}3\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{5}(2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x{|}_{-2}^{0}+({x}^{2}+3x){|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =[3(0)-3(-2)]+[({5}^{2}+3(5))-({0}^{2}+3(0))] \\\\  & =6+25+15 \\\\  & =46.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
